   "the_two_questions_this_page_answers": {
-    "a_prognosis_by_partner": "\u26d4 NO POOLED MAGNITUDE. \u26a0 *Superseded, retained: 'MOVED on 2026-08-08 ... the outcome pool is now two non-overlapping cohorts and 73 patients, and a crude magnitude for disease-specific death exists for the first time.'* That rested on Huang 2023 Table 1 cells no retained original verifies, and they are withdrawn (2026-09-08). What the record supports is ONE source-verified cohort's recorded per-partner event counts and observation windows, with four other series reported separately at their own scope. No independent prognostic effect, no equivalence and no size-confounding explanation is established. See analyses.B_outcome_by_partner.",
+    "a_prognosis_by_partner": "\u26d4 NO POOLED MAGNITUDE. \u26a0 *Superseded, retained: 'MOVED on 2026-08-08 ... the outcome pool is now two non-overlapping cohorts and 73 patients, and a crude magnitude for disease-specific death exists for the first time.'* That rested on Huang 2023 Table 1 cells no retained original verifies, and they are withdrawn (2026-09-08). What the record supports is ONE SERIES IN THE MAIN EVENT ANALYSIS -- Agaram 2014's recorded per-partner event counts and observation windows -- PLUS a separately reported and separately source-verified Sjogren 2003 outcome context (0/3 TAF15 against 1/5 EWSR1 recorded tumour-related deaths), with three further series described at their own abstract scope. No independent prognostic effect, no equivalence, no null, no signed follow-up bias and no size-confounding explanation is established. See analyses.B_outcome_by_partner.",
     "b_treatment_response_by_partner": "\u26d4 AN IMPRECISELY ESTIMATED RESPONSE ASSOCIATION, NOT AN ABSENT ONE. \u26a0 *Superseded, retained: 'a zero-event arm yields no magnitude at any denominator', and 'zero of five is not a rate'.* BOTH ARE MATHEMATICALLY FALSE and are withdrawn (2026-09-08). Zero responses among three or five patients IS an observed proportion with a very wide uncertainty interval, and the TAF15-minus-comparator differences of recorded response proportions are computed in analyses.A_tki_objective_response like any other contrast on this page. What is true is narrower and is the actual limit: the differences are imprecise, the comparator arm's own point estimate lies inside the TAF15 arm's interval in both analyses, and a treated-only comparison between partner groups -- at any denominator -- CANNOT establish that the partner modifies treatment benefit. That needs a treatment comparator and a treatment-by-partner analysis, or a carefully bounded alternative design, and neither exists in this record. What would narrow the proportions is a further cohort reporting objective response by partner with integer counts, or the Lancet Oncol 2019 full text's partner distribution.",
-    "why_this_block_exists": "Because the two are easy to conflate and the conflation would be an over-claim in the direction the whole page is trying to avoid. A prognostic magnitude is not a predictive one: knowing that TAF15 patients die more often, crudely and probably because their tumours are bigger, says nothing about whether they respond to a drug class. That remains true with the pooled magnitude withdrawn."
+    "why_this_block_exists": "Because the two are easy to conflate and the conflation would be an over-claim in the direction the whole page is trying to avoid. \u26d4 *WITHDRAWN OUTRIGHT 2026-09-08 (residual batch R3), retained as superseded: 'knowing that TAF15 patients die more often, crudely and probably because their tumours are bigger'.* THAT IS THE REJECTED CAUSAL SIZE EXPLANATION and it is not supported by anything in this synthesis: no partner coefficient, interval, event count, model specification or missing-data rule is available in any retained source, and size may itself be a consequence of fusion-driven biology or lie on the causal path between partner and outcome. The point that survives is only the distinction itself: a prognostic contrast among untreated-or-mixed patients and a response contrast among treated patients are different endpoints in different populations, and neither moves the other. That remains true with the pooled magnitude withdrawn."
